From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Thu, 9 Mar 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: the choosing calls, the "send to a player" calls and
 the dice give the empty value of their type when the bound opponent is gone,
 at n > 2

Patch 0059 gave an empty value to the queries and to most actions, but the calls that choose or send to a player still took
`return 0` and gave no Lua value. A script that uses the answer (`Duel.SelectOption(1-tp,...)+1`,
`Duel.SelectMatchingCard(1-tp,...):GetFirst()`) then raised a Lua error when the bound opponent was eliminated after the bind
(Half or Nothing 15552258 binds 1-tp to the turn player when it is activated; Painful Return 57902193). Owner rule OQ3 says never
a Lua error. Now these calls push the empty value through the fold::gone_* helpers of patch 0059: an empty group for
SelectMatchingCard, SelectTarget, SelectTribute (also for a gone tribute-to player), SelectReleaseGroup (gone tribute-to player)
and SelectFusionMaterial; nil for SelectCardsFromCodes and GetChainMaterial (it returns an effect, not a group); 0 for
SelectOption, SelectDisableField, SelectFieldZone, SendtoHand, SendtoDeck, SendtoExtraP, Sendto, SSet and Duel.RemoveOverlayCard;
false for SelectYesNo, SelectEffectYesNo and CheckReleaseGroup (gone tribute-to player); one 0 per result for TossCoin (count)
and TossDice (count1 + count2). PLAYER_NONE, PLAYER_ALL, the values above 1 and every call with two duelists keep the stock
result (no value), byte for byte: the helpers push nothing outside a fold scope. Duel.GetOverlayGroup, GetOverlayCount and
CheckRemoveOverlayCard already gave the empty value (a dead seat is still a seat there) and are not changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UrYy4jjEcbJHKdcVYasfdb
